  "pattern": "type-coercion",
  "difficulty_rating": 1675,
  "explanation": "The if (r.value) guard coerces the value to a boolean, and numeric 0 is falsy. The zero reading is a legitimate measurement but is skipped by the present counter, so the count prints as 2 even though the summed total is 11 — a mismatch that only tracing each value exposes.",
  "prompt": "This tallies readings, counting how many are present and their total. Step through and predict the printed count and total.",
  "language": "javascript",
  "snippet": "function slotTotals(readings) {\n  let sum = 0;\n  let present = 0;\n  for (const r of readings) {\n    if (r.value) present += 1;\n    sum += r.value;\n  }\n  console.log(`${present} readings, total ${sum}`);\n  console.log(\"sum:\", sum);\n}\nslotTotals([{ value: 4 }, { value: 0 }, { value: 7 }]);",
